1
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten it up,
then step back and take a look.

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,620
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
hand in hand with Gā-chan.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,440
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:47,680
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:01,760
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

8
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the aunties who are a thorn in your side too.

9
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning that corner over there.

10
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kameari surely Kameari.

12
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:32,940
Everyone, come on over to our town!

13
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

14
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:39,800
Hyper President's family service.

15
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,340
Janken-bō!

16
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,200
I lost again.

17
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,720
Well then, see you on that course.

18
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,060
That's right.

19
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:53,240
Even every day would be pretty good

20
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:53,940
That's right.

21
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:57,600
It hasn't changed a bit since we were kids.

22
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:02,120
I once got stuck carrying fifteen
people's worth of school backpacks!

23
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:03,660
That many?

24
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:05,940
I couldn't see ahead,
so I fell into the river.

25
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:07,960
We really got a lot of flak from everyone.

26
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:11,500
Sounds like your childhood, senior.

27
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:14,180
Kids are better off being innocent,
you know.

28
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:17,180
This is fine, thanks.

29
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:19,220
Who are you?

30
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:21,060
Aren't you Denkyoku Plus-kun?

31
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:23,360
It's that cop from before.

32
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,980
Does a grade schooler like
you even have money for a taxi?

33
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,680
I don't have any money.

34
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:30,940
I'll pay with a taxi ticket.

35
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:31,580
Yes.

36
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:34,460
Don't go acting like some salaryman.

37
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,280
I make it a rule not to carry cash.

38
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,620
Everything's by card.

39
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:41,500
Ugh, you cheeky brat.

40
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,460
Hey, you're a grade schooler with no income,

41
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:46,880
how do you even have a credit card?

42
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,720
No, I do have income.

43
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:52,340
I hold the rights to a game
software I came up with.

44
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:56,040
He had an income of about 20 million yen.

45
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,740
20 million yen.

46
00:02:58,260 --> 00:02:59,640
For an elementary school kid,

47
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,320
that's more than my annual salary!

48
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:03,220
This damn cocky brat!

49
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,700
Senpai, please calm down.

50
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,440
His father is

51
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:09,720
the president of Super Denshi Koki, so

52
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,920
he's good with computers, you know.

53
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,000
So what's that supposed to mean?

54
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,820
Anyway, for an elementary school kid,

55
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:18,080
Excuse me for a moment.

56
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,160
It's me.

57
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:21,620
Yeah.

58
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:23,120
I'm busy with some family matters right now,

59
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:27,280
and you're still talking like a grown-up

60
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:30,720
Did you keep the test
questions on the host by email?

61
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:34,380
OK, I'll download them right
away and call you over there.

62
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,560
So this is the high-tech randoseru!

63
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:40,860
It's a lot thinner than
the randoseru I saw before.

64
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:44,320
High-tech devices are advancing day by day,
after all.

65
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,200
What are you doing?

66
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:51,080
I'm connecting it to a cell phone to
download data from the other party.

67
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:55,720
Now he's copying the data
to an electronic organizer

68
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:57,480
What an unpleasant elementary schooler.

69
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:04,860
There, that's done.

70
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:09,040
But once he puts his randoseru on, he's
just an ordinary elementary schooler again.

71
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:12,380
What is he planning to do this time?

72
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:19,080
Looks like he's using it for navigation.

73
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:22,420
Well, I have work to do,
so I'll be taking my leave.

74
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:25,240
Hey, what do you mean, work?

75
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,940
Is that a police stop-and-question?

76
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:31,880
Don't throw around jargon,
you're just an elementary schooler.

77
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:36,620
He'll show up around that
corner any moment now.

78
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:50,960
Plus-kun, why are you here of all places?

79
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:54,100
We got a call from your father.

80
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:58,780
He said you ran away from home with Plus-kun,
so we were asked to stop you.

81
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:04,100
Well, if he'd come himself it would be one thing,
but making his son do that is the lowest.

82
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,520
Mom, I'm not going back.

83
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:09,060
Mom, it's no use running anywhere.

84
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:14,960
That car has a tracking device, so we
can easily navigate to wherever you are.

85
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:18,620
Well then, I have a plan of my own.

86
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:21,680
Let's go, Plus-kun.

87
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,200
Mom, it's no use.

88
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,660
Plus-kun has a tracking device on him too.

89
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:29,600
Why, hey!

90
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:32,780
You're scary!

91
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:35,420
Please calm down, Mom.

92
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:38,700
Let's keep this calm and
talk it over rationally.

93
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:40,180
Phew.

94
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,100
I can't take it anymore.

95
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:46,580
Please look at this.

96
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,700
What is this?

97
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:53,460
It looks like just kindergarten merchandise,
but...

98
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:54,760
But,

99
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,200
it's a computer.

100
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:01,060
Since we're entering the information age,

101
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:04,000
even kindergartners
should have one at least.

102
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,480
Plus, be quiet.

103
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,120
Yes.

104
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:08,860
And also DVD players and...

105
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:16,480
It even has a mini microwave in the lunchbox,
and he said the beret is for safety.

106
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:18,120
It even has tear gas hidden inside.

107
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:26,480
It's the small version of the high plan, you know.
My husband uses minus at the company just like plus.

108
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:32,080
He's using it as a monitor for a new product his company developed,
so I understand why he'd want to use it at home.

109
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:37,620
I feel like... right? I've become a completely
high-tech person and lost my emotions.

110
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:49,160
I don't want him to become a minus like the plus.
Look, my mother and brother are trying to do it at home, yet he takes his own classes over the internet.

111
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,360
Well, I can't take this anymore!

112
00:06:52,640 --> 00:07:02,800
Please don't get so worked up. I'm the one who's being inconvenienced by your marital quarrel.
Oh well, later I'll have my cram school friends download the lesson content.

113
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:04,420
That's just how Banji is.

114
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,160
This child doesn't have
any childlike emotions.

115
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:09,620
Just the other day, too.

116
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:13,940
Plus-chan, look at this.

117
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:15,540
This flower is pretty, isn't it?

118
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,160
Please wait a moment.

119
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:21,260
The correct name is campanula, Mom.

120
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:23,700
It's an angiosperm.

121
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:30,140
Plus has lost the ordinary feeling of
looking at a flower and thinking it's pretty.

122
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:32,380
It's all just information and knowledge.

123
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:34,160
T-true enough.

124
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:35,420
Right?

125
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:39,340
Alright, I'll go see Senshuya
and give him a piece of my mind.

126
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:40,320
Really?

127
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:42,400
Yeah, I'll really tell him off.

128
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:46,940
Understood.

129
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,840
Then send it to the design
department right away.

130
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:52,980
So the new product is good to go, right?

131
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:53,880
Next,

132
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,600
Mr. Smith of Microbreak Co., and

133
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:01,100
the preliminary meeting for tomorrow's deal.

134
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:02,100
Mr. President,

135
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:02,980
What is it?

136
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:05,440
Your wife is here to see you.

137
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:06,380
Got it.

138
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:09,520
Please handle contact with Mr. Smith.

139
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:10,080
Yes.

140
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:16,020
Mother.

141
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:18,160
You came back after all.

142
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,620
Good work, Plus.

143
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:20,216
Dear,

144
00:08:20,266 --> 00:08:23,820
I never said a word about going home yet,
you know.

145
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:25,720
Is that so? Plus?

146
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:26,980
Yes, Ryotsu-san.

147
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:29,100
Please leave the rest to us.

148
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,080
Ryotsu, who is he?

149
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:39,040
He's the police officer who tested
the Super Electronic GX767 for us.

150
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:40,880
Ryo-san from back then!

151
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:42,660
Thanks to you testing it as a monitor,

152
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:48,280
the flaws in the Super Electronic GX767 came to light,
and that was a great help.

153
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:50,720
We went through hell back then.

154
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:57,160
Now the Super GX777, with those flaws fixed,
is selling all over the world.

155
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:02,220
It became a huge hit,
with sales topping two million units.

156
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:05,320
It's thinner than yours and looks so cool!

157
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,760
Ryotsu-san.

158
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:10,420
No! I didn't come here to
listen to your bragging.

159
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,720
Stop using your own sons as test subjects.

160
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,180
That's impossible.

161
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:17,540
If we test it elsewhere,
our development will be exposed.

162
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:21,700
I'm doing this with a heartless resolve,
all for researching better products.

163
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:25,460
I have no reason to be
scolded by an outsider like you.

164
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:28,860
Quiet!

165
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:32,380
Is it all right for him to lose the
emotions of a normal elementary schooler?

166
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:37,960
Plus is an eight-year-old elementary schooler,
yet he never laughs or cries.

167
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:44,960
It's all because you made him
test your company's products.

168
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:48,960
At this rate,
he'll grow up to be a heartless person.

169
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:52,000
Before long,
he'll kick you out of the company

170
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,560
and Plus might end up as president.

171
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,360
That would be just fine.

172
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:57,740
What?

173
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:01,920
Our high-tech industry is
truly in a Sengoku-era struggle.

174
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:05,400
If Plus grows up to be that tough,

175
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,400
I'll be satisfied.

176
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:09,740
Ma'am, this father and son are hopeless.

177
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:11,720
You'd better divorce him quickly.

178
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:15,460
Yes. I've decided I'm going back
to my parents' home after all.

179
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:19,320
I love Mom this much,
and you're going to leave me like this?

180
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:23,860
Ryotsu-san, what on earth should I do?

181
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:27,380
I just need to act like a
normal father with Plus, right?

182
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:29,800
Even though you're called a father,

183
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:32,920
like playing catch on your day off,
for example,

184
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,160
Playing catch?

185
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,880
Well, we play all the time, right, Plus?

186
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:37,660
Yeah.

187
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:40,180
I've never seen you do it, though.

188
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:43,540
Is about 130 kilometers
an hour good for the speed?

189
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:44,100
OK.

190
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:46,160
Here I come, Dad!

191
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,140
Nice ball!

192
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:51,680
Alright, now it's Daddy's turn!

193
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:52,880
Here I come, Plus!

194
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:54,520
You idiot!

195
00:10:55,740 --> 00:10:58,140
Who plays catch in virtual reality?

196
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:01,180
I've decided I'm going back
to my parents' home after all.

197
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:02,580
M-Mom.

198
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:03,871
Ryoji,

199
00:11:03,921 --> 00:11:07,220
Isn't there any other way
for Plus and Koboro to bond?

200
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,110
Well, tomorrow's Sunday,

201
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:14,440
how about forgetting studying and work and
spending the whole day at an amusement park?

202
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:17,440
Then, I have virtual amusement
park software right here.

203
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:19,698
No! Not a game!

204
00:11:19,748 --> 00:11:22,260
We play together in person, skin to skin!

205
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:26,560
I see! Then let's go to Katsushika Wonderland with Plus,
just the two of us!

206
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:28,180
That sounds good.

207
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:29,360
That would be a problem.

208
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:32,880
President,
Mr. Smith is arriving in Japan tomorrow,

209
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,460
No, that's out of the question.

210
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:36,700
Tomorrow I'm bonding with my child.

211
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:39,700
Dear, you've finally understood.

212
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,740
Yes, of course.

213
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:43,920
All right, it's a promise!

214
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,900
I'm so glad, Plus-chan.

215
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,760
Well then, shall we go home?

216
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:48,160
Yes.

217
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,080
Thank you for your hard work.

218
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:56,820
The president finally got us
a one-hour business meeting,

219
00:11:56,820 --> 00:12:00,080
so we really need him to sign
the contract by noon tomorrow.

220
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:03,920
Being caught between the
president and the father is tough.

221
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:05,400
Right, negotiation!

222
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:07,760
I see.

223
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,780
Well, that's good news, isn't it?

224
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:16,660
Yeah, but at this rate, they won't
be able to enjoy an amusement park

225
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:19,200
like a normal father and son.

226
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:20,440
Yeah, that's true.

227
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:23,860
Could you keep an eye on those two for us?

228
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,120
I'll give you a reward. Please.

229
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:30,118
A reward? Alright. This territory,

230
00:12:30,168 --> 00:12:32,140
leave it to Kankichi!

231
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:51,660
Just like the navigation said,
there's traffic.

232
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:53,920
It's Sunday, so there's nothing we can do.

233
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:56,220
Dad, at this pace,

234
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:59,680
it'll take 72 minutes to reach
the Wonderland parking lot.

235
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:03,000
Plus, that calculation is a little off.

236
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,200
Let's see it.

237
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,240
This parking lot's capacity is 1,500 cars.

238
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:11,900
According to the internet,
it'll be full in another 120 cars.

239
00:13:12,340 --> 00:13:14,140
Once it's full, they stop letting cars in.

240
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:19,200
From this spot,
our chance of getting in is 52.63%.

241
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:23,140
Right, I forgot to put the
entry restrictions into the data.

242
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:25,140
Knock it off already.

243
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:27,820
We didn't come here to do calculations,
we came to play!

244
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,660
Sorry, out of habit -

245
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,560
Honestly, what kind of parent is this?

246
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,440
Come on, Plus.

247
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:38,320
Wait a minute.

248
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:42,720
You don't need a randoseru
to go out and play.

249
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:46,000
But you might get emails from your friends.

250
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,560
Plus, you're going to have
lots of fun with me today.

251
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:51,580
Leave that stuff behind.

252
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:52,200
Yes.

253
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:54,760
Nakagawa, confiscate it.

254
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:55,760
Yes.

255
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,740
Then let's leave it in the car.

256
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:01,580
Come on, let's play lots, Plus.

257
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:02,220
Wait!

258
00:14:02,620 --> 00:14:02,960
Uh-oh.

259
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:12,100
W-what is this? I only have a video camera.

260
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:15,160
Why are you wearing a suit
when we're just playing?

261
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,040
N-no reason. I just like suits.

262
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:19,380
Change into this.

263
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:21,620
Do I really have to change?

264
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:22,420
Yes!

265
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:24,740
Fine, it can't be helped.

266
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:27,800
What is this thing!

267
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,120
It's a Hyper Business Suit.

268
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:34,460
Every business tool is
built right into the suit.

269
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:36,180
It's a groundbreaking garment.

270
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:37,280
W-wow, this is amazing.

271
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:38,800
This is no time for "but"s.

272
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,340
That's also a recruitment.

273
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:43,480
You have no complaints now, do you?

274
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:45,020
I don't have anything else on me.

275
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:45,840
Is that the truth?

276
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:50,020
Nakagawa, the metal detector.

277
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:50,220
Yes.

278
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:52,800
Come on.

279
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,480
There's something in the belt.

280
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:01,680
Isn't using a metal detector cheating,
you know?

281
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,940
There's a pager built into the buckle.

282
00:15:05,580 --> 00:15:06,300
What else?

283
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,400
A videophone in the shoe sole.

284
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:12,880
The watch is an internet terminal.

285
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,520
And this bean-shaped item is a radio.

286
00:15:16,180 --> 00:15:18,160
Are you James Bond or something?

287
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:35,880
Alright, Plus, today I'm going to be
a normal dad for the whole day, okay?

288
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:38,440
You don't have to force yourself, you know.

289
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:40,620
I'm not forcing myself at all.

290
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:44,460
Welcome, ting-tarah!

291
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:49,400
I know, I'll record you
and Mackie together on video.

292
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,120
Come on, Plus.

293
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,340
Well, that's fine, I guess.

294
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:52,960
Don't do everything.

295
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,720
You're finally starting
to act like a father.

296
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,500
We'll see.

297
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:03,120
I can't get close at all.

298
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:05,460
Listen up, everyone.

299
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:09,040
Shouldn't we keep to the order here and take turns,
one at a time?

300
00:16:09,040 --> 00:16:11,160
Dad, you don't need the video.

301
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:13,760
No, I'll handle it. Wait right there.

302
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:16,680
I have to do something as a father.

303
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,740
Alright then.

304
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,600
I brought Mackey along.

305
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:27,700
Come on, come on.

306
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,320
Now then, Plus.

307
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:31,880
Look, it's with Mackey.

308
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:34,900
I don't care, I don't even like Mackey.

309
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:36,440
Don't say that.

310
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:38,040
You're secretly happy, aren't you?

311
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,080
Come on, smile, smile.

312
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:42,500
Where's the "ordinary dad" in that?

313
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,880
Plus, what do you want to ride next?

314
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,460
Pick whichever one you like.

315
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:49,680
Dad, that's enough already.

316
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:51,760
Then how about we go on a ride next?

317
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:55,280
He's starting to look like a real father,
little by little.

318
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,680
Pretty ordinary, isn't he?

319
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,300
Work comes second, if at all.

320
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:02,180
The more time a child spends
playing with his father,

321
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:04,040
the richer a person he becomes.

322
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:06,020
Looks like he's finally woken up.

323
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:08,700
Damn it!

324
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:10,880
It's time for the meeting with Mr. Smith.

325
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,160
Plus...

326
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:13,660
What is it?

327
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:16,240
Let's shoot a video in
front of that flower bed.

328
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:18,300
Stand over there, in front of that.

329
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:19,160
Understood.

330
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:24,760
It's me.

331
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,940
Mr. President, Mr. Smith is making the deal.

332
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:29,660
Got it, show me the goods.

333
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:30,660
Yes.

334
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:35,520
It's a prototype of fabric
woven with solar cells.

335
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:38,320
How about 10 meters for 10,000 dollars?

336
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:41,340
The performance seems good.

337
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,140
But 10,000 dollars is expensive.

338
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:46,180
Hey, where are you grabbing?
Plus is over here.

339
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,580
Right.

340
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:51,160
Why does the video camera have an antenna?

341
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,880
These flowers are truly beautiful.

342
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:01,160
I really want to get some
shots of the flowers on camera.

343
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,480
Looks like Ryotsu is going to notice.

344
00:18:03,940 --> 00:18:05,400
I'll contact you later.

345
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:09,660
Why are you talking to
yourself into the video camera?

346
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:13,160
No, I registered it together with Mr. Hesse.

347
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:14,800
Hiding it is suspicious.

348
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,160
The video camera is confiscated too.

349
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,180
Not that!

350
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,520
Not that!

351
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,680
No, I just wanted to film lots of Plus-kun.

352
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:26,700
Don't just film me.
Enjoy some of the attractions too.

353
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:30,240
According to what I saw online,

354
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:34,380
at this lunchtime, the roller
coaster is relatively easy to ride.

355
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:36,900
Really? Then let's do that.

356
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:40,300
Oh no, we've kept Mr. Smith waiting.

357
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:43,180
At this rate,
the deal is going to fall through.

358
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:46,980
No choice. I'll give up being
the good dad and make the call.

359
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:52,000
Oh, here comes our company's helicopter.

360
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:54,900
How do I get in touch with...

361
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,300
There it is.

362
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:59,980
Plus, let's play that game together.

363
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:01,860
Yeah, sure.

364
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:05,440
Whoa, Mom got taken out!

365
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,800
Dad, you're really bad at this.

366
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:09,600
Nah, I'm still not good enough.

367
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:10,940
Bang bang, whoa!

368
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,340
You're finally becoming a normal dad.

369
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:14,740
Looks like it.

370
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:15,900
Oki-san.

371
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:18,340
I was worried, so I came anyway.

372
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:24,020
Alright,
maybe I'll shoot that helicopter down.

373
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,860
Whop whop whop whop whop!

374
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:29,880
Tell him ten thousand dollars is too high,
it's eight thousand.

375
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:31,740
Just notice me, will you?

376
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:37,180
Yes, got it!

377
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:40,240
Plus!

378
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:41,440
Roger that.

379
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:41,840
Yes.

380
00:19:45,740 --> 00:19:46,940
Hey, wait!

381
00:19:48,340 --> 00:20:06,580
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!
No no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no!

382
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,300
Come on, no way, not the mountain!

383
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,940
Eeeeeh!

384
00:20:12,940 --> 00:20:14,080
Eeeeeh!

385
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,900
I'm serious, do it!

386
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:21,260
Aaaaaaah!

387
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,860
Hah, you can't run anymore!

388
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:36,180
We'll see about that.

389
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:42,840
Nothing, a helicopter is coming
to pick us up any minute now.

390
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:46,420
Stop! What on earth do you want from us?

391
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:49,200
The thing your company
is developing right now -

392
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:52,300
we want all the data on
the Hyper Learning Figure.

393
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:53,440
W-what?

394
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:56,260
If you care about your son's life,
hand over the data.

395
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,780
I can't right now.
The data is at the company.

396
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:04,920
Shut up! We know you carry
the important data on a disk.

397
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:09,360
Dear, if it's true, hand it over quickly.

398
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:11,740
Mister, it's no use.

399
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:18,300
Dad cares more about the company than his family.
He'll never agree to the deal!

400
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:19,460
That's ridiculous!

401
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:20,520
Honey...

402
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,276
I'm sorry, but -

403
00:21:23,326 --> 00:21:27,320
could you bring me the disk from
the inside pocket of my super suit?

404
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,280
Understood.

405
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:29,240
Honey...

406
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:31,140
That's what a true father is.

407
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:35,440
Nakagawa-san, wait.

408
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:40,120
While you're at it,
please bring my randoseru too.

409
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:42,720
Hey, kid, don't say unnecessary things!

410
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:43,558
Mister,

411
00:21:43,608 --> 00:21:47,160
Do you really think Dad will hand
over the secret data obediently?

412
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:47,540
What?

413
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:51,380
For all you know, the disk might be empty.

414
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,140
Let me check it for you.

415
00:21:53,860 --> 00:21:55,280
W-what are you saying, Plus-kun?

416
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:57,840
I'm not that cold-hearted a man.

417
00:21:57,840 --> 00:21:58,220
Stop it!

418
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:00,800
Kid, you said something good there.

419
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:03,020
Hey, bring the randoseru too.

420
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:08,080
Good, back off!

421
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:11,940
The pickup helicopter just arrived!

422
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,360
How about it, kid?

423
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:18,480
Please, wait!

424
00:22:21,220 --> 00:22:23,380
Looks like it's the real deal.

425
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:24,520
Thank goodness.

426
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:28,280
Now!

427
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:28,640
Yes!

428
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:33,040
You've given us a lot of trouble, damn you.

429
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:36,760
The ferry's getting away!

430
00:22:36,780 --> 00:22:38,080
Come on, take him down!

431
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:48,280
Plus-chan,
I'm so glad you're safe, Plus-chan.

432
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:49,760
Plus.

433
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:50,610
Dad,

434
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:54,800
handing over important
trade secrets just like that

435
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:56,380
you're still too soft, you know.

436
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:58,680
P-Plus.

437
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,287
But I,

438
00:23:00,337 --> 00:23:03,480
I was really happy, Dad.

439
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,920
P-Plus, did you just laugh?

440
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:07,060
Plus.

441
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:10,700
Plus.

442
00:23:18,220 --> 00:23:21,380
He's quite a good father, after all.
I've changed my opinion of him.

443
00:23:22,180 --> 00:23:23,620
Right, Senior?

444
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:30,500
Plus-kun, your dad's the president of a big company, yet he forgets work and plays with you all day.
He's a truly wonderful father.

445
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:32,680
Both of you,
that's going too far with the praise.

446
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:35,140
Just look at his new product.

447
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,560
Wonderland Navigation.

448
00:23:38,140 --> 00:23:41,520
If you put this software on a
pocket computer and carry it around,

449
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:44,860
it tells you right now which
attraction has how many hours of wait,

450
00:23:44,860 --> 00:23:48,920
and even tells you by voice that during
the parade is the best time to go.

451
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:53,120
Wait, he was gathering information
that thoroughly even in that situation?

452
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:56,660
He really is a man with no wasted movement.

453
00:23:56,660 --> 00:23:58,580
Ahahaha!

454
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:14,200
Dash, dash, dash

455
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:19,900
Catching a nap on Dad's
back on the packed train

456
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:26,180
Hard work again this week,
unreasonable demands are only fair

457
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:33,680
Acting cool with a bucket in one hand,
but it's a beef bowl with extra cloudy sauce

458
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:40,580
Endless overtime frustrations,
cleared right up with more frustration

459
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:50,340
Every day is no problem,
once I've passed through the hot shower

460
00:24:50,340 --> 00:24:56,920
Every day is no problem,
my energy restored by a sleep pillow

461
00:25:00,060 --> 00:25:06,560
Every day is no problem,
I really love a girl like me

462
00:25:06,560 --> 00:25:09,400
Every day is no play

463
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:13,340
Hearts flying around on Monday

464
00:25:13,340 --> 00:25:17,300
Man Ray, Man Ray, no play

465
00:25:21,660 --> 00:25:23,980
The Chief got laid off?

466
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:28,580
And after decades as a cop,
he can't do anything else at all, they say?

467
00:25:28,940 --> 00:25:31,240
It can't be helped, it's for my former boss

468
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:33,500
I'll find a part-time job for him

469
00:25:33,500 --> 00:25:36,460
Next time:
swallowing his pride for a part-time job

470
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,540
See you then!

